---
// Teaching yourself: free courses, and earning college credit by exam (CLEP) for little or no money.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SELF_LAUNCHED } from '../lib/site.js';
import { RESOURCE_GROUPS, RESOURCES_CHECKED } from '../lib/learning-resources.js';
const CHECKED = 'November 6, 2026';
const S = {
  cb: { label: 'College Board: Earn College Credit with CLEP', url: 'https://clep.collegeboard.org/' },
  cbReg: { label: 'College Board: Register for a CLEP exam', url: 'https://clep.collegeboard.org/register-for-an-exam' },
  cbExams: { label: 'College Board: CLEP exam topics', url: 'https://clep.collegeboard.org/clep-exams' },
  hacc: { label: 'HACC testing center: CLEP (updated August 2026)', url: 'https://libguides.hacc.edu/learningcommons/testing/CLEP' },
  suffolk: { label: 'Suffolk County Community College: CLEP fees', url: 'https://sunysuffolk.edu/apply-enroll/transfer-students/CLEP/fees.jsp' },
  ms: { label: 'Modern States: FAQ', url: 'https://modernstates.org/faq/' },
  ocw: { label: 'MIT Open Learning: MIT OpenCourseWare', url: 'https://openlearning.mit.edu/courses-programs/mit-opencourseware' },
  khan: { label: 'Khan Academy Help Center: does it cost money?', url: 'https://support.khanacademy.org/hc/en-us/articles/202260114-Does-it-cost-money-to-use-Khan-Academy' }
};
---
<Layout title="Teach yourself: free courses and college credit by exam | After High School"
  description="How to learn on your own after high school: free courses from MIT OpenCourseWare and Khan Academy, and how CLEP exams can earn you college credit for $97 or less, sometimes free."
  path="/teach-yourself" nav="colleges" noindex={!SELF_LAUNCHED}>
  <section class="compare-head">
    <h1>Teach yourself</h1>
    <p>You can learn a lot on your own for free, and some of it can count as college credit later. Here's how credit by exam works, where to learn online, and the catch: what you learn alone only counts when someone recognizes it, so check before you count on it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="clep">
    <h2 id="clep">Earn college credit by exam (CLEP)</h2>
    <p class="block-lede">CLEP exams, run by the College Board, test what you'd learn in an intro college course. Pass one and a college that accepts it gives you credit, so you skip the class and its tuition.</p>
    <dl class="xfer-compare self-facts">
      <div><dt>Exams</dt><dd><strong>34</strong> exams</dd><dd class="xfer-sub">in history and social sciences, composition and literature, science and math, business, and world languages</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Cost</dt><dd><strong>$97</strong> per exam</dd><dd class="xfer-sub">plus a test center fee, for example $20 at HACC or $44 at Suffolk County Community College</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Colleges</dt><dd><strong>Over 3,000</strong></dd><dd class="xfer-sub">grant credit for CLEP, each with its own passing scores and limits</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="block-lede">Anyone can take a CLEP exam, at a test center or at home with remote proctoring, and most scores come right away. If you're in the military, your exam may be paid for by your military benefits. Before you test, look up the college you plan to attend: what score it needs, which exams it takes, and how many CLEP credits it allows.</p>
    <p class="wys-src">Sources: <a href={S.cb.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{S.cb.label}</a>; <a href={S.cbReg.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{S.cbReg.label}</a>; <a href={S.cbExams.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{S.cbExams.label}</a>; test center fees from <a href={S.hacc.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{S.hacc.label}</a> and <a href={S.suffolk.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{S.suffolk.label}</a>. Checked {CHECKED}.</p>

    <h3>Take CLEP for free through Modern States</h3>
    <p class="block-lede">Modern States offers 32 free online courses taught by college professors, with free textbooks, that prepare you for CLEP exams. Finish a course (an average of 75% on its quizzes and at least 75% on its final, with retakes allowed) and you get a voucher that pays the CLEP exam fee. Some test centers still charge their own fee. You need to be 13 or older.</p>
    <p class="wys-src">Source: <a href={S.ms.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{S.ms.label}</a>. Checked {CHECKED}.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="free">
    <h2 id="free">Where to learn online</h2>
    <p class="block-lede">Well-known places to learn on your own, most of them free. They're listed A to Z in each group, not ranked. Nobody paid to be listed, and these aren't affiliate links. The description and cost for each come from its own page.</p>
    {RESOURCE_GROUPS.map((g) => (
      <>
        <h3>{g.title}</h3>
        <ul class="res-list">
          {g.items.map((r) => (
            <li>
              <a class="res-name" href={r.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{r.name}</a>
              <span class:list={['res-cost', { free: r.cost === 'Free' }]}>{r.cost}</span>
              <p>{r.what} <a class="res-src" href={r.source} rel="noopener" target="_blank">Source</a></p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </>
    ))}
    <p class="wys-src">Checked {RESOURCES_CHECKED}. Know a great free resource we should add? Email <a href="mailto:hello@afterhighschool.me">hello@afterhighschool.me</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="count">
    <h2 id="count">Making it count</h2>
    <ul class="xfer-srcs">
      <li><strong>For college credit,</strong> use exams a college recognizes (like CLEP), and check that college's policy first.</li>
      <li><strong>For a job,</strong> show what you can do: a portfolio, projects you built, or a certification employers in that field ask for. Look at real job postings to see which ones they name.</li>
      <li><strong>Building something of your own?</strong> A few <a href="/fellowships">fellowships</a> pay young people to work on their own projects.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep a record.</strong> Save your course list, scores and projects in one place so you can show them later.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
